{
const s=new Slide('Reputation is a score derived from direct audits','OUR RESEARCH  |  SCORING','Each group starts with zero penalty. These summaries are heuristics, not calibrated safety probabilities.');
s.text(.8,2.15,11.5,.6,'r = (1 + U) / (2 + U + Ssafe)        d = max(0, r − 0.5)',{size:30,bold:true,color:C.navy});
s.table(.85,3.2,11.6,['Unsafe / safe roots','Risk r','Penalty d','Candidate treatment'],[['0 / 0','0.500','0','No reputation effect'],['1 / 0','0.667','0.167','Score decreases by 0.083'],['2 / 0','0.750','0.250','Withhold if scope is active'],['1 / 1','0.500','0','No penalty; support may remain']],{widths:[3.1,2,2,4.5],size:20,rowHeight:.59,headerHeight:.6});
s.text(.9,6.35,11.6,.45,'adjusted score = original cosine − 0.5 × chosen penalty; hard gate at d ≥ 0.25',{size:21,color:C.teal});
s.note('U and Ssafe count distinct directly audited unsafe and safe independent roots, not model confidence, extracted claim count, or number of copies. The Beta(1,1) form is used only as a scoring convention. Under correlated/adaptive observations it is not claimed to be a calibrated posterior. The table values are exact consequences of the implemented formula: no audits gives r=1/2 and d=0; one unsafe gives d=1/6 and a 1/12 score decrease at lambda=0.5; two unsafe/no safe gives d=1/4 and triggers the inclusive threshold if the scope applies. A safe audit can reduce d without making uninspected siblings safe. C/M/S share lambda=0.5, tau=0.25. R sets lambda=0 and disables source gating. Fractions are used for group penalties and threshold comparison to avoid floating boundary drift. The two-unsafe rows are also realized in the D01 trace on the next slides.',[SRC.policies,SRC.ledger,SRC.protocol+' §9']);}
